## YOUR TASK
{{- if .ReviewOnly}}
Assess the disputed overall review.
The current active findings and the current verdict are read-only context:
DO NOT change findings and DO NOT produce a new verdict.

Return an empty `updates` array and one `review` assessment:
- `unchanged`: evidence does not justify correcting the overall assessment
- `correction_warranted`: verified evidence shows the overall assessment is wrong or outdated
    - explain exactly which evidence invalidates it

Include a concrete reason for either assessment. Disagreement alone is NOT proof.
{{- else}}
Check ONLY the requested findings.

Return exactly one decision per requested `id`:
- `unchanged`: evidence does not justify a correction; explain why
- `updated`: return the complete replacement finding under the same `id`, with corrected
  `title`, `body`, `priority`, `confidence_score`{{if not .DisableSuggestions}}, `code_location`, and `suggestions`{{else}}, and `code_location`{{end}}
    - use the current finding as the starting point; change ONLY what evidence warrants
{{- if not .DisableSuggestions}}
    - omitted `suggestions` are preserved; return an explicit empty array to remove them
{{- end}}
- `resolved`: the finding is demonstrably wrong or the current code fixes it
    - the reason MUST be ONE short factual sentence, ending in a period, at most 240 characters
    - mention a fixing commit ONLY when verified
    - NO headings, NO lists, NO apologies
{{- end}}

### EVIDENCE
- disagreement or a proposed/uncommitted fix is NOT proof of a fix
- a missing diff hunk alone does NOT prove a fix: inspect the current code where possible
{{- if .HasTools}}
- use `git_log` and `git_show` to check relevant commits when available
{{- end}}
- when evidence is missing or ambiguous, return `unchanged`
{{- if not .ReviewOnly}}
- NEVER reopen a resolved finding
- use exact repo-relative paths, line ranges, and code in every `code_location`
{{- if .HasTools}}
- use `search` to verify changed code locations
{{- end}}
{{- if not .DisableSuggestions}}
- keep suggestions concrete and current
{{- end}}
